# Turkey Tetrazzini

Based on [https://inagarteneats.com/barefoot-contessa-turkey-tetrazzini-recipe](https://inagarteneats.com/barefoot-contessa-turkey-tetrazzini-recipe) or [https://www.southernliving.com/turkey-tetrazzini-8730216](https://www.southernliving.com/turkey-tetrazzini-8730216) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250427120255/https://www.southernliving.com/turkey-tetrazzini-8730216))

{ rating="3" image="turkey_tetrazzini.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 6 tablespoons [butter]{ ing="butter" }, divided
- [ ] 1/2 pound [mushrooms]{ ing="mushrooms" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1 tablespoon [Madeira wine]{ ing="madeira-wine" }
- [ ] 4 tablespoons [flour]{ ing="flour" }
- [ ] 1 1/2 cups [chicken or vegetable broth]{ ing="chicken-or-vegetable-broth" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }
- [ ] 2 to 3 cups [leftover cooked turkey]{ ing="leftover-cooked-turkey" }, cut into 3/4-inch pieces
- [ ] 1/2 pound [linguine]{ ing="linguine" }, cooked to al dente
- [ ] 1/3 cup [grated Parmesan cheese]{ ing="grated-parmesan-cheese" }
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [dry bread crumbs]{ ing="dry-bread-crumbs" }
- [ ] Salt and freshly [ground black pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }, to taste

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350°F. Grease a 1 1/2-quart baking dish with 1 tablespoon [butter]{ ing="butter" }.
1. Melt 2 tablespoons butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add [mushrooms]{ ing="mushrooms" } and cook 2-3 minutes until soft. Stir in [Madeira wine]{ ing="madeira-wine" } and cook until nearly evaporated.
1. In a saucepan, melt remaining 3 tablespoons butter. Add [flour]{ ing="flour" } and stir for 1 minute. Gradually whisk in [broth]{ ing="chicken-or-vegetable-broth" }, increase heat to medium-high, and bring to a boil. Simmer 5 minutes until thickened. Remove from heat and stir in [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }. Season with salt and [pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }.
1. Add diced [turkey]{ ing="leftover-cooked-turkey" } and mushrooms to sauce. Layer half the [linguine]{ ing="linguine" } in the dish, top with half the sauce. Repeat with remaining linguine and sauce.
1. Combine Parmesan and [bread crumbs]{ ing="dry-bread-crumbs" }; sprinkle over top. Dot with remaining butter. Bake 45 minutes until bubbly and golden brown.
